        "body": "Resolves #1623\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n- **RFC 9110 §13.1.2 Compliance:** When evaluating conditional requests with `If-None-Match`:\n  - For safe methods (`GET`, `HEAD`, and `QUERY` per RFC 10008), a matching entity tag resolves to `304 Not Modified`.\n  - For other methods (such as `POST`, `PUT`, `DELETE`, `PATCH`), [RFC 9110 §13.1.2](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9110#section-13.1.2) specifies that the recipient MUST NOT perform the requested method and SHOULD generate a `412 (Precondition Failed)` response. Previously, `handleCacheHeaders` unconditionally emitted `304`.\n- **RFC 9110 §13.1.3 Compliance:** `If-Modified-Since` MUST be ignored if the request method is neither `GET` nor `HEAD` (or `QUERY`). For non-safe methods (like `POST`), `If-Modified-Since` without `If-None-Match` no longer halts execution or returns `304`/`412`.\n- **RFC 9110 §13.2.1 Compliance:** Conditional headers are ignored for `OPTIONS`, `TRACE`, and `CONNECT`.\n- **Tests:**\n  - Added unit tests in `test/utils.test.ts` verifying `412` for `POST`/`PUT` with matching `If-None-Match`, `304` for `GET`, ignoring `If-Modified-Since` for `POST`, and ignoring conditional headers for `OPTIONS`.\n  - All 3,118 tests pass across the repository.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Conditional cache requests now return the appropriate status for different request methods: matching validators return 304 for GET, HEAD, and QUERY, and 412 for other methods.\n  * `If-Modified-Since` is applied only to GET, HEAD, and QUERY. Conditional cache headers are ignored for OPTIONS, TRACE, and CONNECT.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
